descriptions.job-0piv6db:
&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an enthusiastic, motivated, and technically curious individual—with an IT operations focus—to join Jane Street’s IT Security team, and contribute to securing our firm&#39;s IT computing platforms and identities. This will involve technical hands-on work, creative problem-solving, and collaboration across teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional responsibilities of this role will include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploying, documenting, and implementing security controls at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as a key component to our Vulnerability Management program to ensure we’re detecting and mitigating vulnerabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing guidance and support to the broader IT department and IT Operations team as security incidents arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing both technical and non-technical solutions in collaboration with engineering teams to address security concerns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to the development of our team’s operational playbooks and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who loves collaborating alongside others, enjoys triaging complex problems, and is able to delegate and escalate tasks effectively. This role is anything but siloed—you will be a key communicator, translating complex technical issues for various audiences while maintaining a high level of technical accuracy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we’re open to individuals from a range of backgrounds, someone who’s worked in a code-driven or declarative environment and has hands-on experience with security incident response is preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 5-7 years of experience as a security or operations engineer, with a technical background rooted in Windows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can maintain, support, and administer Windows, macOS, and hybrid identity platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have demonstrated knowledge of typical attack patterns, adversary methods, and protective technologies utilized to mitigate related risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooter and debugger; familiar with trending and log analysis, and have hands-on experience using system performance tools to identify production disruptions&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can deploy and implement Endpoint Security controls in highly available environments (e.g., application control, log aggregation, host-based firewalls, EDR, disk encryption)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can use PowerShell scripting to automate security tasks and to analyze data at an intermediate level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communicator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to navigate ambiguity and changing priorities with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and approachable; eager to be a team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Having knowledge of macOS security fundamentals is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out to agency-partnerships@janestreet.com.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

descriptions.job-1v962tb:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: NY, Chicago, or London&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded 19 years ago and headquartered in Chicago, the DV Group of financial services firms has grown to more than 450 people operating throughout the world. Since spinning out of a large brokerage firm in 2016, DV Trading rapidly scaled as an independent proprietary trading firm utilizing its own capital, trading strategies, and risk management methodologies to provide liquidity and hedging opportunities to financial participants, commodity producers and counterparties worldwide. DV Group affiliates also include two broker dealers, an introducing broker in commodities, a cryptocurrency market making firm, and several investment advisory firms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a senior &lt;strong&gt;Vice President / Director – US Futures Sales &amp;amp; Asset Manager Coverage&lt;/strong&gt; to drive growth across our &lt;strong&gt;US futures platform&lt;/strong&gt;, with a primary focus on expanding relationships with asset managers. This role is designed for a commercially driven professional who can combine strong client connectivity with a strategic, market-facing approach to positioning and distributing futures capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with trading, research, and leadership teams to increase visibility, deepen engagement, and grow revenue across asset management clients while maintaining exposure to broader futures markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue growth across &lt;strong&gt;US-listed futures and options&lt;/strong&gt;, with a focus on asset managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and expand relationships with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asset Managers (macro, fixed income, CTA, systematic)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select hedge funds and institutional investors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a market-facing ambassador for the firm’s futures capabilities, products, and execution strengths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with trading teams to position strategies, spreads, basis, rolls, and execution solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new distribution opportunities and under-penetrated client segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate client outreach, presentations, and targeted marketing initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the firm at client meetings, conferences, and industry events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–15+ years of experience in &lt;strong&gt;US futures sales, asset manager coverage, or institutional derivatives marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at an &lt;strong&gt;FCM, bank, asset manager, or futures brokerage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong, existing relationships with &lt;strong&gt;asset management firms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to grow &lt;strong&gt;client engagement, volumes, and revenues&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US futures markets (CME and related venues)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rates, equity index, and/or commodity futures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client workflows, margining, and clearing structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating at a &lt;strong&gt;VP / Director or equivalent senior level&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
